  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive). Pattern: X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{滅|ほろ}びる.\n\nTRANSITIVE PAIR: ⟦{滅|ほろ}ぼす→滅ぼす：13332_horobosu⟧ (to destroy, to annihilate).\n\nUSAGE:\n{滅|ほろ}びる describes large-scale destruction or extinction — civilizations falling, species dying out, kingdoms collapsing. It is not used for small everyday things breaking. The word carries a literary, dramatic tone.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{国|くに}→国：02204_kuni⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{滅|ほろ}びる: a country falls\n- ⟦{文明|ぶんめい}→文明：03611_bunmei⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{滅|ほろ}びる: a civilization perishes\n- ⟦{種|しゅ}→種：28584_shu⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{滅|ほろ}びる: a species goes extinct\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n⟦{滅亡|めつぼう}→滅亡：13360_metsubou⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ is the ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧-verb equivalent meaning \"to perish/be annihilated,\" often used in news and historical writing.",
